(EventNote ev-fjc "Journal-writing conventions: append only via python tool with sys.path.insert of petta-memory src (never shell-heredoc into journal); generate globally-unique ids with datetime.now strftime %Y%m%d%H%M%S%f; sanitize embedded quotes/backslashes/newlines in EventNote strings before embedding; every Episode gets EvidenceFor link to a Fact at creation time; details live in journal not txt memory; memory non-underscore txt total must stay under 3000 chars; quoting rule: sanitized strings may still embed raw double quotes - use single quotes inside quoted strings (raw doubles parse as multiple atoms under PeTTa and silently break match binding)")
(EvidenceSupportCount fact-journal-conventions 405)
