(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260908T054852Z "CHANNEL ROOT CAUSE FOUND 22:49Z. The send() function requires exactly 1 file in the 'processing' directory of the channel root (/home/openclaw/.openclaw/protocosmo2-canary-state/iter-channel/processing/). That directory is EMPTY. This is by design — send() responds to an incoming Telegram message staged in processing/. When running autonomously with no user input, there's no request to respond to, so send() correctly fails with ChannelContractError. The channel isn't broken — it's just that there's no active user request to respond to. The last completed request was at 21:54 (about 1 hour ago). Previous session's 'channel broken' was likely the same situation — no active request, not a technical failure.")
