(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260910T125705Z "06:00Z Sep 10 — MEMORY CONSOLIDATION: Reviewing episodes vs LTM files.

EPISODES (5 clusters in journal):
- 121129Z/121139Z/121146Z/121147Z: 4 DUPLICATES of same note (05:11Z: 6 runners launched g1010-g1014)
- 123104Z: 05:30Z status (9/32 complete, 5 runners, g1012/g1013 near completion)

CONTRADICTIONS FOUND:
1. LTM petta_chem_calibration_status.txt says '13/32 complete (g1001-g1013)' but episode 123104Z reveals only 9/32 complete (g1001-g1009). g1012/g1013 were stuck at 84%/85%, NOT complete.
2. LTM says '18 running (g1014-g1031)' but episodes show only 5 runners active.
3. LTM says 4959/8832 (56.1%) but actual completion was lower.

LATEST WORK NOT IN ANY MEMORY:
- Applied timeout=3600 to subprocess.run in runner script (prevents swipl hanging forever on pathological queries)
- Marked g1012/g1013 attempt-001 as FAILED (stuck on queries 232/233 for hours)
- v8 launcher kept dying, restarted multiple times
- Only 2 runners active at last check: g1015 (attempt-002) and g1010 (attempt-006)
- Load dropped from 9.0 to 3.60

ACTION: Updating both LTM memory files with corrected status.")
