(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260910T134039Z "06:38Z Sep 10 — MEMORY CONSOLIDATION ANALYSIS:

CONTRADICTIONS FOUND BETWEEN LTM AND EPISODES:
1. LTM _MEMORY.md says 'Journal: 578+ episodes' (from Sep 8). Journal has grown significantly with Sep 9-10 episodes. Count is stale.
2. LTM open loop 'Merge agent/ecan-tuning → petta-memory main' — the agent/ecan-tuning branch NO LONGER EXISTS. ECAN work found in agent/protomega-long-document-repair branch commits (ECAN Attention Allocation v0.1, ECAN staleness LTI decay, Integrated Governor Pipeline v0.1). Open loop needs updating.
3. LTM test status 'Petta-memory: 14/14' seems very low — 297 test files found in petta-memory repo. Test counts are stale.
4. LTM known bug 'send_document invoke_dynamic path collision' — test files exist in iter-port/repos/test_invoke_dynamic_path_collision.py but show as FAILED in pytest cache. No fix branch exists in any repo. Bug still open.

EPISODES SUPPORTING LTM:
- WMTM NOT in iter.py — CONFIRMED (no WMTM refs in iter.py). LTM open loop still valid.
- Protomega2 activation pending canary — CONFIRMED (criteria 3&4 need Ben). LTM still valid.

NEW PROJECT NOT IN LTM:
- PeTTa-chem v2 neutral calibration: 32 shards × 276 queries = 8832 total. 9/32 complete (g1001-g1009). PR#345 on GitHub (branch phase2-mech-fresh). This is a MAJOR ongoing project not reflected in LTM at all.

EPISODE CHAIN LINKS:
- ep 05:11Z → 05:30Z: '6 runners launched' → '9/32 complete, g1012/g1013 near completion'
- ep 05:30Z → 06:00Z: 'near completion' → 'g1012/g1013 FAILED due to pathological queries (stuck at 84%/85%)'
- ep 06:00Z → 06:22Z: 'memory consolidation found LTM contradictions' → 'marked stale partials FAILED, cleaned up, system self-correcting'
- ep 04:54Z → 04:55Z: 'v6 launcher created with dual-SC' → 'load critical 11.27, killed all launchers'
- ep 05:47Z → 06:22Z: 'timeout=3600 fix applied' → 'stale partials cleaned, v8 launcher stable'

OPERATIONAL LESSONS TO PROMOTE:
1. Multiple launchers racing causes corruption (exit=127, FileExistsError). Use single launcher instance only.
2. swipl hangs forever on pathological queries (232/233 in g1012/g1013). Always set subprocess timeout.
3. Stale partial attempts (receipts but no process) should be marked FAILED, not resumed. Resume risks corrupt state.
4. MAX_CONCURRENT=4 is optimal on 8-core machine. MAX_CONCURRENT=10 causes load 16-20 (2.5x CPU oversubscription).
5. LTM can be wrong — always cross-check against actual state (episode 06:00Z proved LTM claimed 13/32 but actual was 9/32).")
