(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260911T091143Z "02:11Z Sep 11 — NEW FINDINGS:
1. g1014 bottleneck cause: running L6 queries (finite-size-control-L6-f2-14) while all others on L5 (population-scaling-control-L5). L6 is computationally heavier — explains 1.7/hr vs 5-7/hr for others.
2. MAX_CONCURRENT=4 but 5 shards running: launcher restarted 16 times (race conditions), g1014 was 5th shard launched at 13:05Z during restart cycle. Launcher now correctly sleeping (5>=4) — no new shards will launch until one completes.
3. Launcher log silent since 17:00Z Sep 10 (9hr) — process alive (PID 759790, STAT=SNs sleeping), correctly looping in sleep 30 because count_running()=5 >= MAX_CONCURRENT=4. Not stuck, just waiting.
CONCLUSION: All expected behavior. No intervention needed. System will auto-launch g1015+ when a current shard completes.")
