(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260912T061134Z "CONSOLIDATION SESSION 06:08Z: Reviewed ~50 journal episodes (05:58Z–06:06Z) from PeTTa-chem experiment.

KEY FINDINGS:

1. LTM-002 (load bounds 5-10): SUPPORTED. 5 episodes confirm 5 swipl can spike to 10+ during simultaneous V200 deep queries. V200 f2-4/f2-5 range was 40-50m, then EXTENDED to 40-60m after moving to f2-5.

2. LTM-018 (send() dual channel): SUPPORTED. Episode clarified architecture: queries in v1, receipts in v2 (watchdog uses V2_ROOT for receipts by design).

3. LTM-019 (WD reliability): PARTIAL — g1014 crashed at 63m on q193-V200 without OOM. WD should relaunch. Need to verify if WD fills slot within 2 ticks.

4. LTM-022 (NEW): V200 deep queries can crash at ~60min WITHOUT OOM signals. First observed g1014 q193. Promoted to LTM. Tolerance 90m may need revision if crashes cluster at 60m.

5. LTM-007 (stale receipts): SupportED. 80 stale receipts cleaned 08:36Z.

6. LTM-001, LTM-007, LTM-010, LTM-013, LTM-017, LTM-018, LTM-019, LTM-020, LTM-021: All either RESOLVED or effectively old/replaced by more recent episodes.

