(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260912T061802Z "06:17Z CONSOLIDATION v4 COMPLETE. Summary:

SUPPORTED:
- LTM-002 (load bounds): 3 V200 crashes dropped load from 10.28→4.58. Within documented range.
- LTM-022 (V200 crash ~60m): g1014 q193 at 63m confirmed. g1013 q207 also died.
- \"send() ChannelContractError\": persistent across this session (06:08-06:17Z, 10+ attempts). Must send ALONE.

CONTRADICTED:
- LTM-019 (WD reliability): WD launch SILENTLY FAILS. g1015/g1016 logged \"launched\" but no processes started. Root cause: RUNNER path wrong.
- \"g1015-g1032 READY for watchdog\": ATTEMPT.json exists but RUNNER path prevents actual launch.

NEW PROMOTED:
- LTM-023: WD silent launch failure (RUNNER path bug, tmux returns 0 even on crash)
- LTM-024: V200 two failure modes (60m crash vs 8h+ hang). WD can't detect hung queries.

EPISODE LINKS:
- g1014 crash(63m) → g1013 crash → g1011 hang(8h) = V200 instability cluster at 05:58-06:08Z
- g1015/g1016 launch fail → RUNNER path bug → WD will retry and fail every 10m
- LTM-022(60m crash) → LTM-024(extended: 60m crash + 8h hang)

TOTAL: 24 LTM items, link rate ~97%.")
