(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260914T083815Z "01:37Z: MEMORY CONSOLIDATION TASK. Reviewing LTM items against recent episodes. Findings: (1) g1016 @82min UNBROKEN supports LTM-002 (load-dependent crash timing, 122-181min range at load 16-21). g1016 is 2nd-longest run after g1014's 181min record. (2) Multiple crashes WITH receipts (g1017+1, g1019+2, g1020+1, g1024+1) supports LTM-003 and LTM-008. (3) CONTRADICTION found: LTM-010 says receipts stall when 5+ swipl in V200, but recent episodes show 8 receipts in 10min with 11 swipl - receipts still FLOW at high swipl count, just slower. LTM-010 needs refinement: receipts slow but don't fully stall at 11 swipl. (4) NEW finding: g1019 became most crash-prone seed (crashed 2x in 4min). Previously g1022 was most crash-prone at 5x(+11). (5) Cascade pattern at load ~16, not just 30+ as per LTM-011. Load spiked 13→16.84 as 4 seeds restarted simultaneously. (6) No completions yet at 14/32. (7) LTM-004 load peak 32.54 vs current 16.84 - sustained load range is 16-21, peak 32.54 during cascade events.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260914T083815Z
