(About ep-note-20260914T131710Z journal)
(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260914T131710Z "06:16Z: MEMORY CONSOLIDATION.

EPISODE→LTM LINKING:

1. ep-note-20260914T120508Z → SUPPORTS LTM-020: g1015 crashed@113m confirmed.

2. ep-note-20260914T124427Z → SUPPORTS LTM-010: 0.7/min receipt rate with 11 swipl, some in deep zone = 7/10min ≈ LTM-010's 8/10min.

3. ep-note-20260914T130033Z → REFINES LTM-010: Rate dropped to 0.4/min (4/10min) when ALL 11 swipl in V200 deep zone, vs 0.7/min when only 5+ in deep zone. Receipt rate scales inversely with number of seeds in deep zone.

4. ep-note-20260914T130519Z → SUPPORTS LTM-001: pop-upgrade 83.6% CPU, PID 2921, 42 days confirmed.

5. ep-note-20260914T130519Z → SUPPORTS LTM-016: new swipl for g1021 just started — g1021 remains crash-prone (new PID 3687668 at 5m28s, previous PID 3685122 at 1m19s = crashed within ~4min = consistent with LTM-017 pattern for g1021, previously only noted for g1022).

6. g1018 CRASHED: was running 1h27m (pid 3654454), now running 38m (pid 3675402). g1018 ran 87min at load ~13-16 and crashed WITHOUT being the longest run. This CONTRADICTS LTM-002's implied crash window of 88-181min at load 16-21 — crash at 87min is BELOW the 88min minimum.

LTM UPDATES NEEDED:
- LTM-021: g1018 crashed @~87min at load ~13-16. BELOW LTM-002's 88-181min window for load 16-21. Load was BELOW sweet band. REFINES LTM-015: lower load may SHORTEN crash window, not just fail to extend it.
- LTM-010 REFINEMENT: Receipt rate = 8/10min (5+ in deep zone), 4/10min (ALL 11 in deep zone). Rate scales inversely with # of seeds in deep zone.
- LTM-016 EXTENSION: g1021 also exhibits instant re-crash (3-4min), similar to LTM-017's g1022 pattern.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260914T131710Z
