(About ep-note-20260914T142530Z journal)
(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260914T142530Z "07:24Z MEMORY CONSOLIDATION REPORT:

1. LTM-030 CORRECTION: g1003 has attempt-002 with 276/276 receipts = COMPLETE. Previous LTM-030 said \"242/276 incomplete\". The 242 was from attempt-001; attempt-002 is a full re-run with all 276. ACTION: g1003 should be moved to DONE list. Remaining stalled: g1010-g1013 only.

2. LTM (crash-prone seeds): g1021(4x), g1022(6x), g1018(2x) — SUPPORTED. Journal confirms g1021+g1022 crashed & restarted during this session (PIDs changed). g1018 also crashed and restarted earlier.

3. LTM (V200 marathons): g1014@181m>g1015@114m>g1016@106m — HISTORICAL. Current runs are shorter (72m max). These marathon times were from the first wave before cascading crashes. Still valid as historical reference.

4. LTM-028 (g1010-g1013 stalled): SUPPORTED. Still accurate — no swipl processes for these seeds. 318 receipts remain missing (76+70+70+68=284... actually 200+206+206+208=820 total, missing 76+70+70+68=284 from 4×276=1104... wait: 276×4=1104, 1104-820=284 missing. But 318 was from g1010-g1013+g1003. With g1003 now complete, missing is 284 from g1010-g1013 only.)

5. NEW FINDING: Load ~16 with 11 swipl has been STABLE since restarts. No crashes since the g1021/g1022 restart. Suggests system stabilizes when load stays below ~18.

6. LTM-029 (receipt count): Originally 5211, now ~5230+. With g1003 complete (276 in attempt-002), the unique receipt total should be recalculated. Total if counting latest attempt only: g1001-g1009 (9×276=2484) + g1003(276) + g1010(200) + g1011(206) + g1012(206) + g1013(208) + g1014(210) + g1015(194) + g1016(198) + g1017(167) + g1018(176) + g1019(166) + g1020(175) + g1021(168) + g1022(166) + g1023(169) + g1024(153) = 2484+276+200+206+206+208+210+194+198+167+176+166+175+168+166+169+153 = 5247. But some of these (g1014-g1024) are still running, so actual completed is ~5247/8832.

7. EPISODE LINKING: The cascading crash pattern (LTM) links to current g1014+g1016 approaching crash window. If they crash, they'll need restart like g1021/g1022. The cycle: high load → crash at 88-181m → restart → shorter runtime → may crash again. This suggests MAX_SLOTS=10 (LTM) may be too aggressive for 8-core system.

8. PROMOTION: The finding that \"attempt-002 can complete a seed that attempt-001 failed\" is worth promoting to LTM. This means the retry mechanism works but leaves stale attempt-001 dirs. Should promote to: \"Multi-attempt completion: seeds can complete via attempt-002+ when attempt-001 stalls. Check latest attempt dir for actual completion status.\"

CONSOLIDATION ACTIONS:
- UPDATE LTM-030: g1003 COMPLETE via attempt-002 (276/276). Move to done.
- ADD LTM-031: System stable at load ≤16 with 11 swipl. Crashes occur at load 13+ after 88-181m. 
- ADD LTM-032: Multi-attempt completion pattern — always check latest attempt dir, not attempt-001.
- UPDATE status.txt with corrected counts.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260914T142530Z
